<h2 class="design">Advocacy Journalism</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">The paper with three names tries something different</h4>

<p>

Former Times Herald-Record publisher Jim Moss: "And there's a question for us at the newspaper. Do we simply hold up a mirror and report dispassionately about what we see, or is there a positive, albeit less objective, role for us? <br />
The accompanying editorial report is where we came down on this question. <br />
This report required our open minds. It required research and discussions with scores of Newburgh residents. But it is not a news story bound by journalistic requirements of objectivity. Indeed, we come to this as people and as a business with a rooting interest in the this city."<br />
Thus, this report <a href="http://recordonline.com/news/special_reports/newburgh/">Promised Land,</a> from John Doherty and Tim Logan. It's a great read, and I'd love to know what you all think about crossing the line. Tim, John, how did you feel about it?<br />

