<br />
They haven't been his. But he was there. He was close enough to see the bride's hand tremble. He doesn't know what brings them to this moment, when he pronounces them husband and wife. And he doesn't know what will happen when they leave.<br />
<br />
Huffman just says the words he transcribed from a scene in a black-and-white movie long ago:<br />
<br />
"To have and to hold, from this day forward, for better or for worse, for richer or for poorer ..."
