strips of siding that slap and groan in the <br />
warm breeze, across a silt-browned lawn that <br />
once received a lot of care, and peer through <br />
the beveled glass of someone's front door. This <br />
is what you see: black mold several feet up the <br />
white walls and three-quarters up the carpeted <br />
stairs; thrown furniture wearing a mucky <br />
veneer; and mud on the floor that is still <br />
