<h2 class="design">Love you, miss you, drive safe, peace</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Mike Dawson with a tale</h4>

<p>

He asked for some Gangrey feedback on <a href="http://www.recordonline.com/archive/2006/05/21/news-madcoriann-05-21.html">his chilling story</a> of a girl named CoriAnn McDevitt: <br />
<br />
The party started at 7 p.m. It's already 7:10, and 13-year-old CoriAnn McDevitt's jeans are still damp.<br />
<br />
Though her closet's stuffed with jeans, she wants the off-white Hydraulics she bought two weeks ago at the Palisades Center. They're the only ones to wear to this Friday night party.<br />
<br />
Boys will be there.<br />
<br />
"Throw them back in the dryer for 10 minutes and I'll run you right over," her mother, Theresa, tells her.<br />
<br />
Ten minutes go by.<br />
<br />
The ding-dongs of "Final Jeopardy" ring from her parents' first-floor bedroom where Kevin, her father, lies half-dozing on the bed. Then, the "Wheel of Fortune" theme song.<br />
<br />
Theresa, tall and thin with long, black hair, stands at the top of the basement stairs. A hint of cigarette smoke creeps from the nearby enclosed porch, where she likes to toke her Marlboros.<br />
<br />
She only hears the rumbles of the Whirlpool dryer.<br />
<br />
"CoriAnn."
