<br />
The hand he extended had five perfectly manicured nails.<br />
<br />
"Mitch Rogovin."<br />
<br />
"Maureen Dabbagh."<br />
<br />
"Come in," the man said. "A pleasure to meet you."<br />
<br />
The room was large and rectangular, colorless and cold, with a desk that nobody seemed to use.<br />
<br />
On the far side of the room was a conference table. Around it sat three men.<br />
<br />
Rogovin said, "These boys used to be Special Forces." One, he said, was a Navy SEAL, another an Army Ranger, the third a Green Beret. "They're retired," he added, smiling, "on paper."<br />
<br />
Maureen reached for her shoulder bag to pull out the paperwork on her kidnapped daughter, Nadia. Rogovin stopped her. "No need," he said. "I've got your file."
