<h2 class="design">Does He Still Love Me?</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">Welcome Home</h4>

<p>

Read Erin Sullivan's <a href="http://pqasb.pqarchiver.com/sptimes/access/1165610791.html?dids=1165610791:1165610791&FMT=FT&FMTS=ABS:FT&date=Nov+20%2C+2006&author=ERIN+SULLIVAN&pub=St.+Petersburg+Times&edition=&startpage=1&desc=Welcome+home">story</a>: Since he's been gone, their puppy has grown into a dog who sleeps on his side of the bed.<br />
<br />
Andy and Danielle Mercer were newlyweds when he went to war. Andy, 24, spent their first anniversary in Southern Iraq. Danielle, 25, stayed busy. Any time she stopped, she cried.<br />
<br />
She couldn't function if she allowed herself to feel her pain and fear and loneliness, so she just kept moving.<br />
<br />
Since he's been gone, she's visited Mexico and North Carolina. She's been on a church trip to Kentucky. She's changed jobs. She's gotten a cat, a big fluffy boy she named Max. The air conditioning at their house broke.<br />
<br />
She ate dinner at a girlfriend's house a few times a week and stayed as long as she wanted because there was nothing to come home to.
