<br />
Its rounded end fits into a clear socket containing two electrodes. From there, two wires lead to the computer.<br />
<br />
Boy and machine: a single circuit.<br />
<br />
Greg Bauer, the prosthetist, asks him: "Are you ready for the moment of truth?"<br />
<br />
"Yes," Jonathan whispers. He's been looking forward to this all week.<br />
<br />
On the computer screen is a red bar. When Jonathan flexes one muscle in his elbow, the bar will jump.<br />
<br />
Jonathan leans forward, looking down at his arm.<br />
<br />
He concentrates.<br />
<br />
Nothing happens.<br />
<br />
"All right, my man," Bauer says. "This is going to take a little bit of focus."
