<p>

Read his <a href="http://www.latimes.com/news/nationworld/nation/la-na-trail10mar10,0,6557387.story?coll=la-home-headlines">story</a>: HIS wife and daughter were murdered last summer on a remote hiking trail 70 miles from home, in the middle of the day, at the height of their lives, among mountains they had always regarded as a sanctuary.<br />
<br />
David Stodden doesn't know who did it or why. He doesn't know whether his wife and daughter were beaten, raped or mutilated; whether they fell quickly or fought to the end. He knows the essentials, that each was shot in the head and left just off-trail where anybody could see them. He knows detectives have made no arrests, and hikers all over the region remain shaken. For many, the wilderness itself was desecrated.<br />
<br />
