<br />
Look at this, Mom.<br />
<br />
Mom, look.<br />
<br />
Christie Brazier hears her little girl say this a lot. Sarah is 6. Sarah forgets what happened. She thinks her mom is the same as before, except for the short hair and the long white cane.<br />
<br />
&#8220;I tell her, &#8216;Close your eyes and look around. That&#8217;s what I see.&#8217; I know it&#8217;s really hard for her to understand. That&#8217;s what I tell Sarah to do &#8212; &#8216;Close your eyes and look around.&#8217;&#8221;<br />
<br />
Christie smiles. Her face is turned to the voice of a visitor who sits in the living room of her parents&#8217; home. Christie&#8217;s mom, seated in another chair, brought her home from an Omaha care center a few days ago.<br />
<br />
Christie&#8217;s hazel eyes are dilated. They look oddly dark.</i>
