Jane and I were having Solstice, now we need a place to stay."<br />
And her Christ-loving uncle watched his wife hang Mary on a tree, <br />
He watched his son hang candy canes all made with red dye number three.<br />
He told his niece, "It's Christmas Eve, I know our life is not your style," <br />
She said, "Christmas is like Solstice, and we miss you and it's been awhile,"<br />
<br />
So the Christians and the Pagans sat together at the table,<br />
Finding faith and common ground the best that they were able, <br />
And just before the meal was served, hands were held and prayers were said, Sending hope for peace on earth to all their gods and goddesses.<br />
