<h4 class="byline">clicks</h4>

<p>

<a href="http://www.sportsline.com/collegebasketball/story/10567327">Gary Parrish</a>: THATCHER, Ariz. -- Tim Parmeter pulled into the driveway and clicked and clicked and clicked his garage door opener, probably pushed the thing four or five times, best he can remember. But the door never opened. So he shook his head. <br />
<br />
He just thought his estranged wife had changed the code like she had changed the locks, because that's the kind of stuff people do when they're going through a divorce. And it was a messy divorce.  <br />
<br />
<a href="http://www.kansascity.com/sports/colleges/story/428158.html">Bill Reiter</a>: FORT LAUDERDALE, Fla. | The Virginia Tech marching band walked from the hotel to the dark parking lot out back, and the warm breeze blew off the ocean as the students laughed and talked about what they&#8217;d do once they got some free time.<br />
<br />
Anchored yachts in canals encircled them, as did the palm trees they played under. The water shined as the students got ready to practice for their final performance of the season in tonight&#8217;s Orange Bowl.<br />
<br />
So much had happened already. The shooting, the killings, losing one of their own, the endless questions and talk about what happened and, finally, what comes next. The talk of what you do when one terrible day in your life threatens to define it.<br />
<br />
And, lest you think we only like sports writing, <a href="http://www.desmoinesregister.com/apps/pbcs.dll/article?AID=/20080109/NEWS/801090391">Nigel Duara</a>: Sioux City, Ia. -- Inside the bare interview room at the police department, Marla Harris and her husband were left alone with a desk and two chairs.<br />
<br />
The last thing Harris' husband said to her will be what she remembers as long as she lives.<br />
<br />
"He said he was doing it to protect my son," the 32-year-old said Tuesday. "He said he was trying to help us."
