<a href="http://gangrey.com/1477">
<h2 class="design">Yankee James</h2></a>
<h4 class="byline">stacking and restacking firewood</h4>

<p>

What a lede. Scratch that. What a story. <a href="http://www.recordonline.com/apps/pbcs.dll/article?AID=/20080220/NEWS/802200341">John Sullivan and Paul Brooks</a>: West Hurley &#8212; In the end, the racist who hated blacks, immigrants and Jews died with a broken heart.<br />
<br />
State police say they are investigating the death of James Leshkevich and his wife, Deborah, as a murder-suicide. Troopers found the couple at their 213 Morgan Hill Road home yesterday, after a friend of Deborah Leshkevich called 911 worried about her welfare.<br />
<br />
Leshkevich headed the local chapter of the white supremacist group National Alliance, based in West Virginia. In 2005, he helped Hal Turner, the host of a now-defunct white supremacist radio talk show, organize a rally in Kingston, after a publicized attack by a black student on a white student.<br />
<br />
State police said troopers entered the house at around 11 a.m. and found James, 52, dead in the garage and Deborah, 54, dead in a bedroom. No further details of the investigation, including cause of death, were released yesterday as police removed the bodies to be autopsied.<br />
<br />
Leshkevich regularly vented his opinions on radio shows, as well on a blog site on which he called himself "Yankee James." In the most recent entries, he ranted about catching his wife cheating on him.
